title Three doors, three probes
prompt Keaton -- pair the diff so both mantra rows close
think Started toward the pairing and checked one thing first, which is what the last two laps taught me: does the terminated append even produce a REPLACEMENT? It does not. It is a middle insert, so the pairing could never have reached %689.
obs THE PAIRING IS BUILDABLE AND IT IS NOT THE CRUX. Walking the kept-line marks gives a clean rule -- within each gap between anchors, the nth delete pairs with the nth insert -- and that decides WHICH delete an insert replaces. What it cannot do is let the answer be written down.
obs THREE WAYS TO INHERIT A PLACE, THREE PROBES, THREE REFUSALS. Inherit it whole and the identity collides, since LineId is a subset of Place. Inherit the position with a fresh site and it collides too, because main.rye binds cli_site to ONE constant -- the CLI is one hand, and that is the only case it has.
obs Inherit the run with a fresh position and the counter only rises, so the new line stands above every held line and lands at the END of the run. That is the symptom itself, reached from the other side.
obs SO THE RULING NEEDS A LINE TO CARRY AN ORDER KEY DISTINCT FROM ITS IDENTITY. Today Line holds pos, site and run, and both questions read the same two fields. That is a v3 record, and from_v1 already walked the lawful path.
obs ONE HALF IS PROVEN AND READY: swapping the comparison to run, pos, site orders the replacement correctly and disagrees with the current order on ZERO pairs of existing data, because a run carries one site by construction.
obs I DID NOT BUILD IT. A storage format holding real weaves is not a thing to widen at the end of a long session, and two builds tonight were saved by measuring first. Naming the cost exactly is worth more than a half-right format.
loom probes inherit_whole_collides=true fresh_site_collides_same_hand=true fresh_pos_lands_at_end=true order_swap_disagreements=0
loom rows mantra_open=2 blocking_change=v3_record cli_sites=1
rota none -- a ruling measured on Keaton's word, no rota this lap
file construction/REDS.md both rows carrying the complete diagnosis and the one change that unblocks them
scope the pairing rule found, three inheritance doors closed by probe, the blocking change named as a v3 record
status GREEN -- reds_pin_capacity green, no mantra source changed on disk, every claim a probe
recommend check in (Keaton) -- both rows need one thing: a line that says where it goes without saying who it is
